  "assessment": "The two variants showed bounded RSS oscillation across 60 same-process repetitions. VmHWM rose during allocator/process warm-up and then plateaued in the final ten repetitions; final observed peaks were about 25 MiB in both variants. No continuous monotonic growth was observed in this bounded window. This trace does not explain the separate approximately 5 MiB difference measured in shorter fresh-process runs.",
  "limitations": [
    "VmRSS/VmHWM are process-level observations and do not identify allocation sites.",
    "Reading /proc and retaining trace rows adds small measurement overhead; timing results from these runs are not used for speed comparisons.",
    "Two seeds and one workload were checked; this does not characterize all workloads or allocator configurations.",
    "The allocator may retain freed pages, and the observed peak is not equivalent to live application memory."
  ],
